{title: How Lonely Sits the City}
{subtitle: Lamentations 1}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro (instrumental)}
| [Am] | ×15

{start_of_verse: Intro}
The roads to Zion mourn
For a com[G]forter is far [Am]from me
One to revive my spir[G]it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
How lone[Am]ly sits the city
That was [G]full of people
[Am]How like a widow she has become
She who [Am]was great among the nations
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
She [G]weeps bitterly in the [Am]night
Tears on her cheeks
Among all [C]her lovers
She has [G]none to comfort her
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For these [Am]things I weep
My eyes flow with tears
For a [Am]comforter is far from me
One to re[G]vive my spirit
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]The roads to Zion mourn
For none come to [G]the festival
All her gates are [C]desolate
Her priests [G]groan
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For these things I weep
My [Am]eyes flow with tears
For a comforter is [Am]far from me
One to revive my spirit
{end_of_chorus}

